<header class="article-header article-header-row">
  <h1 title="Security Device Types" class="article-title">
    Security Device Types
    
  </h1>

  <div class="accordion-controls">
    <button type="button" class="accordion-expand-all">
      Expand all
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="accordion-collapse-all">
      Collapse all
    </button>
  </div>
</header>

      
      
      

      <section class="article-info">
        <div class="article-content">
          <div class="article-body">
            <aside v-if="tocLinks.length" id="toc">
              <h4 class="toc-title">Also in this article...</h4>
              <ol class="toc-links">
                <li v-for="link in tocLinks">
                  <span class="toc-link" v-on:click="scrollTo(link.id)">{[{link.label}]}</span>
                </li>
              </ol>
            </aside>

            <div class="geo">
<strong>Geography</strong>: This article is applicable for ANZ Transactive Global customers banking in all ANZ geographies.<br>Full details are available in <a href="https://help.online.anz.com/hc/en-au/articles/28789004096025" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Features by Geography</a>.</div><div class="info">It is a requirement that security device approvers must have Know Your Customer (KYC) information registered with ANZ to approve payments, direct debits and trade transactions. For more information, please refer to <a href="https://help.online.anz.com/hc/en-au/articles/35663566206105-Digital-Services-Security-Features" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digital Services Security Features.</a>
</div><h4 id="h_01J5FH7ARKDYS6R84M5FKBTYP9">About Two-Factor Authentication</h4><p>It is important that you and your organisation take responsibility to stay protected from ever-changing cybersecurity threats. An effective measure to maintain application security is to use multi-factor authentication when accessing and performing high risk tasks such as payment approvals and managing user permissions.</p><p>Both security device types provide Two-Factor Authentication (2FA), which gives you an additional layer of security using a combination of something known (in the form of a password) and something you have (in the form of a security device). Security devices are not required for all users, but ANZ strongly recommends the use of a security device at all times.</p><p>ANZ offers mulitple security device types for use with ANZ Transactive Global:</p><h4 id="h_01HSVVRMWQJJ7QH9XHSQCCFA7H">ANZ DIGITAL KEY</h4><table style="padding: 0px; width: 100%; border-width: 0px !important; border-style: initial !important; border-image: initial !important; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: auto;">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 61.2857%; vertical-align: top;">
          <ul>
            <li>
              A downloadable App, enabling use of your mobile device
              as a security device
            </li>
            <li>
              Log on using your preferred identification method;
              Face ID, Fingerprint or PIN
            </li>
            <li>
              Upon log on, allows individual users to accept or decline
              transactions or Get Rate
            </li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="wysiwyg-text-align-center" style="width: 38.5715%;">
          <img src="/hc/article_attachments/43031032952217" alt="Banker Brief ADK image1.png" width="138" height="285">
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table><h4 id="h_01HSVVRMWQFV8CP1TBW0TRA4ET">TOKEN</h4><table style="padding: 0px; width: 100%; border-width: 0px !important; border-style: initial !important; border-image: initial !important; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: auto;">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 60.4285%; vertical-align: top;">
          <ul>
            <li>A small device resembling a calculator</li>
            <li>
              Generates a One Time Password (OTP) to enter when logging
              on and/or performing important banking transactions
            </li>
            <li>Issued to an individual user and protected by a PIN</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="wysiwyg-text-align-center" style="width: 39.4286%;">
          <img src="/hc/article_attachments/12282972592281" alt="Black_Security_Device.png">
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table><p> </p><!-- related content cards --><div class="related-content">
<h3 id="h_01J3Z4C15D115EGZV9FA5NBMW5">You may find these helpful</h3>
<div class="related-cards">
<div class="related-card">
